From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:06:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] WebAssembly port, Node: RexxAPI shared between processes

Under Node the API server runs as a daemon (rexx.js --orx-wasm-rxapi,
started on first use like rxapi, outlives the session) reached over a Unix
domain socket (rexxapi/common/platform/unix/SysNodeConnection), so external
data queues, registrations and the macrospace are shared between WASM
processes, as natively.  The data path writes to the socket fd directly
and reads through a receive ring, without round trips to the JS main
thread.  ORX_WASM_RXAPI=inprocess keeps the in-process server; it is also
the fallback if the daemon cannot be reached.  rxqueue and rxsubcom are
multi-call tools of the rexx executable (launchers from wasm/build-node.sh);
getpid()/getppid() return the real process ids under Node (the daemon keys
sessions by pid).  qualify-node-cli.sh checks queues across processes.
